editorialMd:
The working idea

The readings are sorted ascending. Pair the first and last, then the second and second-last, until they meet. Produce each pair's sum in encounter order; an unpaired middle reading is recorded unchanged.

Return how many values in the derived sequence are even, including 0 and negative even values.

Why this works

Each derived value follows the unit's stated order and includes exactly the items allowed by its definition. The receipt then folds or filters those values without changing their meaning. Check the empty, singleton, repeated and maximum-size inputs before trusting the final total.

Target time O(n); space O(n).

javascript
function facingCardsEvenKeyCensus(readings, k) {
  const a=readings; let out=[];
  for(let l=0,r=a.length-1;l<=r;l++,r--)out.push(l===r?a[l]:a[l]+a[r]);
  return out.filter(x=>x%2===0).length;
}


